#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/making-a-doctors-appointment.ts:16
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid ""
"Booking a doctor’s appointment usually involves a short conversation with a "
"receptionist. You may need to provide your name, explain the general reason "
"for the visit, choose an available time, and confirm practical details such "
"as the location and required documents.\n"
"\n"
"You do not need to describe your complete medical history to the "
"receptionist. A brief and clear explanation is usually enough to help them "
"choose the correct appointment type.\n"
"\n"
"This roleplay is for language practice only. It does not provide medical "
"diagnosis or treatment advice. If you believe you are experiencing a "
"medical emergency, contact your local emergency service instead of waiting "
"for a routine appointment.\n"
"\n"
"## Start the Call\n"
"\n"
"You can begin with:\n"
"\n"
"- “Hello, I’d like to make an appointment.”\n"
"- “I’m calling to book an appointment with a doctor.”\n"
"- “I’d like to schedule a medical consultation.”\n"
"- “I need to make an appointment for my child.”\n"
"- “I’d like to arrange a follow-up appointment.”\n"
"- “I was asked to call and schedule another visit.”\n"
"\n"
"The receptionist may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Are you already a patient at this clinic?”\n"
"- “May I have your name?”\n"
"- “What is your date of birth?”\n"
"- “Which doctor would you like to see?”\n"
"- “What is the reason for the appointment?”\n"
"- “When are you available?”\n"
"\n"
"## Provide Your Personal Details\n"
"\n"
"The receptionist may need information to find or create your patient "
"record.\n"
"\n"
"You may be asked for:\n"
"\n"
"- Your full name\n"
"- Your date of birth\n"
"- Your telephone number\n"
"- Your address\n"
"- Your patient or insurance number\n"
"- Your email address\n"
"- The name of your regular doctor\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “My name is Alex Dmowski.”\n"
"- “My date of birth is the twelfth of May, nineteen ninety.”\n"
"- “I’m already registered at the clinic.”\n"
"- “This will be my first appointment here.”\n"
"- “Could you check whether my details are already in the system?”\n"
"- “My phone number has recently changed.”\n"
"- “Could I spell my surname for you?”\n"
"\n"
"When spelling information over the phone, you can say:\n"
"\n"
"> “That’s D as in Delta, M as in Mike…”\n"
"\n"
"To confirm numbers:\n"
"\n"
"- “That is one-five, not five-zero.”\n"
"- “Let me repeat the number.”\n"
"- “Did you get the complete phone number?”\n"
"- “Could you read that back to me?”\n"
"\n"
"## Explain the Reason for the Appointment\n"
"\n"
"The receptionist usually needs a short description to determine the "
"appropriate doctor, appointment type, and urgency.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’ve had a cough for several days.”\n"
"- “I have been experiencing back pain.”\n"
"- “I’d like to discuss a recurring headache.”\n"
"- “I need a routine check-up.”\n"
"- “I need to renew a prescription.”\n"
"- “I’d like to discuss some test results.”\n"
"- “I need a follow-up after my previous appointment.”\n"
"- “I have a skin problem that I would like a doctor to examine.”\n"
"- “I need a medical certificate.”\n"
"- “I’d like to ask about a vaccination.”\n"
"- “I’m calling about a problem that started yesterday.”\n"
"\n"
"A useful structure is:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’ve been experiencing [general symptom or problem] for [length of "
"time], and I’d like to see a doctor.”\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’ve been experiencing pain in my shoulder for about a week, and it is "
"not improving.”\n"
"\n"
"You do not need to give intimate or highly detailed information to the "
"receptionist. You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “It’s a private medical issue.”\n"
"- “I would prefer to discuss the details directly with the doctor.”\n"
"- “Could you note that it concerns a personal health matter?”\n"
"- “Is a general description enough for the booking?”\n"
"\n"
"## Explain How Urgent It Is\n"
"\n"
"The receptionist may ask whether the problem is urgent.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “It is not an emergency, but I would like to be seen soon.”\n"
"- “The symptoms are getting worse.”\n"
"- “I’m in significant discomfort.”\n"
"- “I’m concerned because the problem has continued for several days.”\n"
"- “A doctor asked me to arrange an urgent follow-up.”\n"
"- “I think a routine appointment is sufficient.”\n"
"- “I’m not sure how urgent it is.”\n"
"- “Could a nurse call me to discuss whether I need an earlier appointment?”\n"
"\n"
"The receptionist may offer:\n"
"\n"
"- A routine appointment\n"
"- A same-day appointment\n"
"- An urgent appointment\n"
"- A telephone consultation\n"
"- A video consultation\n"
"- A nurse consultation\n"
"- An appointment with another available doctor\n"
"\n"
"The receptionist is not always qualified to diagnose the problem. Their "
"role is usually to collect enough information to direct you to the "
"appropriate service.\n"
"\n"
"## Understand Emergency Instructions\n"
"\n"
"A medical office may tell you to contact emergency services instead of "
"waiting for an appointment if your symptoms appear immediately dangerous.\n"
"\n"
"During a real call, follow the clinic’s instructions. Do not rely on a "
"language-learning simulation to decide whether a situation is an emergency.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Do you think I should wait for an appointment?”\n"
"- “Should I speak with a nurse first?”\n"
"- “Is there an urgent care service I should contact?”\n"
"- “Could you repeat the emergency instructions?”\n"
"- “Which number should I call?”\n"
"- “Could you tell me the name of the service?”\n"
"\n"
"If you believe there is an immediate danger to someone’s life or safety, "
"contact the local emergency service.\n"
"\n"
"## Choose the Right Appointment Type\n"
"\n"
"Different concerns may require different types of appointments.\n"
"\n"
"Common options include:\n"
"\n"
"- **Routine appointment** — for a non-urgent medical concern\n"
"- **Urgent appointment** — for a problem that needs quicker assessment\n"
"- **Follow-up appointment** — to review progress after an earlier visit\n"
"- **Telephone consultation** — a conversation with a doctor by phone\n"
"- **Video consultation** — an online appointment with video\n"
"- **In-person consultation** — a visit at the clinic\n"
"- **Nurse appointment** — for services such as dressings, injections, or "
"some routine checks\n"
"- **Specialist appointment** — a consultation with a doctor in a specific "
"medical field\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Do I need an in-person appointment?”\n"
"- “Could this be handled by telephone?”\n"
"- “Is a video consultation available?”\n"
"- “Should I book with a doctor or a nurse?”\n"
"- “Do I need a referral to see the specialist?”\n"
"- “Can any doctor help me, or should I see my regular doctor?”\n"
"- “How long is the appointment?”\n"
"- “Is this the correct type of appointment for my issue?”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask for a Specific Doctor\n"
"\n"
"You may want to see your regular doctor or a doctor with a particular "
"specialty.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’d prefer to see Dr. Avery.”\n"
"- “Is my regular doctor available?”\n"
"- “I have seen Dr. Avery about this problem before.”\n"
"- “Could I book with a female doctor?”\n"
"- “Could I book with a male doctor?”\n"
"- “Is there a doctor who speaks English?”\n"
"- “I need an appointment with a dermatologist.”\n"
"- “Could I see any available doctor?”\n"
"- “I’m happy to see another doctor if I can get an earlier appointment.”\n"
"\n"
"The receptionist may respond:\n"
"\n"
"- “Your regular doctor is not available this week.”\n"
"- “Another doctor can see you tomorrow.”\n"
"- “The earliest appointment with Dr. Avery is next Tuesday.”\n"
"- “You will need a referral before seeing that specialist.”\n"
"\n"
"## State Your Availability\n"
"\n"
"Be specific about the dates and times that work for you.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’m available on Monday afternoon.”\n"
"- “I can come any morning this week.”\n"
"- “Do you have anything after five?”\n"
"- “I’m not available before three.”\n"
"- “Could I come during my lunch break?”\n"
"- “I would prefer the earliest available appointment.”\n"
"- “Is there anything available today?”\n"
"- “Do you have an appointment tomorrow morning?”\n"
"- “I can be flexible with the time.”\n"
"- “I’m available every day except Thursday.”\n"
"\n"
"The receptionist may offer:\n"
"\n"
"> “We have an appointment on Wednesday at 10:20 or Friday at 3:45.”\n"
"\n"
"You can respond:\n"
"\n"
"- “Wednesday at 10:20 works for me.”\n"
"- “Could you check whether anything earlier is available?”\n"
"- “Friday would be better.”\n"
"- “Unfortunately, I’ll be at work then.”\n"
"- “Do you have anything later in the day?”\n"
"- “I’ll take the earliest option.”\n"
"\n"
"## Confirm Dates and Times Carefully\n"
"\n"
"Dates and times can be difficult to understand over the phone. Always "
"confirm them.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Did you say Tuesday the fourteenth?”\n"
"- “Was that 9:15 or 9:50?”\n"
"- “Could you repeat the time slowly?”\n"
"- “So the appointment is on Friday at half past two, correct?”\n"
"- “Could you use the twenty-four-hour time?”\n"
"- “Is that appointment in the morning or the afternoon?”\n"
"- “Could you send me a confirmation message?”\n"
"\n"
"It is useful to repeat the final details:\n"
"\n"
"> “Let me confirm: Tuesday, July fourteenth, at 3:30 with Dr. Avery.”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About the Location\n"
"\n"
"Some clinics operate in more than one building or location.\n"
"\n"
"You can ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Which clinic is the appointment at?”\n"
"- “Could you give me the address?”\n"
"- “Which floor should I go to?”\n"
"- “Which reception desk should I use?”\n"
"- “Is the entrance accessible?”\n"
"- “Is there parking nearby?”\n"
"- “How early should I arrive?”\n"
"- “Where should I check in?”\n"
"- “Is the appointment at the main clinic or the specialist centre?”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask What to Bring\n"
"\n"
"Depending on the appointment, you may need to bring documents, medication "
"information, or test results.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “What should I bring with me?”\n"
"- “Do I need identification?”\n"
"- “Should I bring my insurance card?”\n"
"- “Do I need a referral?”\n"
"- “Should I bring my previous test results?”\n"
"- “Do I need a list of my current medications?”\n"
"- “Should I prepare anything before the appointment?”\n"
"- “Do I need to avoid eating before the visit?”\n"
"- “Will you send the instructions by email?”\n"
"\n"
"Do not fast, stop medication, or change treatment based only on "
"assumptions. Ask the clinic for specific instructions.\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Costs and Insurance\n"
"\n"
"You may need to confirm whether the appointment is covered or requires "
"payment.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is this appointment covered by my insurance?”\n"
"- “Do you accept my insurance provider?”\n"
"- “Is there a consultation fee?”\n"
"- “How much will the appointment cost?”\n"
"- “Do I need to pay in advance?”\n"
"- “Can I pay by card?”\n"
"- “Will I receive an invoice?”\n"
"- “Do I need authorization from my insurance company?”\n"
"- “Is there a fee if I cancel?”\n"
"\n"
"The receptionist may need your insurance or patient number to check "
"coverage.\n"
"\n"
"## Request Language Assistance\n"
"\n"
"If you are not confident speaking the local language, ask whether language "
"support is available.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Do you have a doctor who speaks English?”\n"
"- “Is an interpreter available?”\n"
"- “Can I bring someone to help me translate?”\n"
"- “Could the appointment be conducted in English?”\n"
"- “Could you speak a little more slowly, please?”\n"
"- “I understand some Polish, but I may need help with medical vocabulary.”\n"
"- “Could you send the important information in writing?”\n"
"\n"
"Ask in advance whether another person is allowed to join the appointment.\n"
"\n"
"## Ask for Accessibility Support\n"
"\n"
"You can inform the clinic about any accessibility needs when making the "
"appointment.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “I use a wheelchair. Is the clinic accessible?”\n"
"- “I need step-free access.”\n"
"- “I have difficulty hearing over the phone.”\n"
"- “Could the doctor communicate with me in writing?”\n"
"- “I need additional time for the appointment.”\n"
"- “Can someone help me enter the building?”\n"
"- “Is there an accessible toilet?”\n"
"- “Could you note my accessibility needs on the appointment?”\n"
"\n"
"## Book an Appointment for Someone Else\n"
"\n"
"You may be arranging an appointment for a child, family member, or someone "
"you support.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’m calling to make an appointment for my son.”\n"
"- “I’m arranging the appointment for my mother.”\n"
"- “The patient’s name is…”\n"
"- “I have permission to arrange the appointment.”\n"
"- “Does the patient need to speak with you directly?”\n"
"- “Do you need their consent?”\n"
"- “Can I attend the appointment with them?”\n"
"\n"
"Privacy rules may limit what the clinic can discuss without the patient’s "
"consent.\n"
"\n"
"## Reschedule an Appointment\n"
"\n"
"If you cannot attend, contact the clinic as early as possible.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “I need to reschedule my appointment.”\n"
"- “I’m no longer available at that time.”\n"
"- “Could I move the appointment to another day?”\n"
"- “Do you have anything available next week?”\n"
"- “Could I change it to a telephone consultation?”\n"
"- “I would like to keep the same doctor.”\n"
"- “What is the earliest alternative appointment?”\n"
"\n"
"You may need to provide:\n"
"\n"
"- Your full name\n"
"- Your date of birth\n"
"- The original appointment date\n"
"- The doctor’s name\n"
"- Your patient or booking number\n"
"\n"
"## Cancel an Appointment\n"
"\n"
"To cancel, say:\n"
"\n"
"- “I need to cancel my appointment.”\n"
"- “I will not be able to attend.”\n"
"- “The appointment is on Monday at two.”\n"
"- “Could you confirm that it has been cancelled?”\n"
"- “Is there a cancellation fee?”\n"
"- “Do I need to book another appointment now?”\n"
"- “Could you send me a cancellation confirmation?”\n"
"\n"
"Cancelling early may allow another patient to use the appointment.\n"
"\n"
"## Join a Cancellation List\n"
"\n"
"If no suitable appointment is available, ask whether the clinic has a "
"waiting or cancellation list.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could you add me to the cancellation list?”\n"
"- “Please contact me if an earlier appointment becomes available.”\n"
"- “I can come at short notice.”\n"
"- “How will you contact me?”\n"
"- “How quickly would I need to respond?”\n"
"- “Could you keep my current appointment while I wait for an earlier one?”\n"
"\n"
"## Handle an Unavailable Appointment\n"
"\n"
"The receptionist may say:\n"
"\n"
"- “There are no appointments available today.”\n"
"- “The doctor is fully booked.”\n"
"- “The next available appointment is in two weeks.”\n"
"- “Your regular doctor is currently away.”\n"
"- “We only have telephone appointments available.”\n"
"\n"
"You can respond:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is another doctor available?”\n"
"- “Could I speak with a nurse?”\n"
"- “Is there another clinic I can contact?”\n"
"- “Could you add me to the cancellation list?”\n"
"- “What should I do if the symptoms get worse?”\n"
"- “Is there an urgent care service?”\n"
"- “Could I have a telephone consultation first?”\n"
"\n"
"## Confirm the Appointment\n"
"\n"
"Before ending the call, confirm:\n"
"\n"
"- The patient’s name\n"
"- The doctor or healthcare professional\n"
"- The date\n"
"- The time\n"
"- The appointment type\n"
"- The location or call method\n"
"- Anything you need to bring\n"
"- Any preparation instructions\n"
"- The cancellation policy\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could we confirm all the details?”\n"
"- “Who will I be seeing?”\n"
"- “Is this an in-person or telephone appointment?”\n"
"- “Will the doctor call me, or should I call the clinic?”\n"
"- “Which number will the doctor use?”\n"
"- “Should I arrive early?”\n"
"- “Will I receive a text or email confirmation?”\n"
"- “What should I do if I need to cancel?”\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Appointment Conversation\n"
"\n"
"A typical conversation may look like this:\n"
"\n"
"> **Receptionist:** Good morning. Dr. Avery’s office. How can I help?  \n"
"> **Patient:** Hello, I’d like to make an appointment, please.  \n"
"> **Receptionist:** Certainly. Are you already registered with the clinic?  "
"\n"
"> **Patient:** Yes. My name is Alex Dmowski.  \n"
"> **Receptionist:** Thank you. What is the general reason for the "
"appointment?  \n"
"> **Patient:** I’ve had pain in my shoulder for about a week, and it is not "
"improving.  \n"
"> **Receptionist:** Would you like an in-person appointment?  \n"
"> **Patient:** Yes, please. Do you have anything available this week?  \n"
"> **Receptionist:** We have Thursday at 11:20 or Friday at 4:10.  \n"
"> **Patient:** Friday at 4:10 would be better.  \n"
"> **Receptionist:** That will be with Dr. Avery at our Central Clinic.  \n"
"> **Patient:** Great. Should I bring anything with me?  \n"
"> **Receptionist:** Please bring identification and a list of any "
"medication you currently take.  \n"
"> **Patient:** Let me confirm: Friday at 4:10 at the Central Clinic with "
"Dr. Avery.  \n"
"> **Receptionist:** That’s correct.\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Appointment Formula\n"
"\n"
"Follow this structure when booking:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Request:** Say that you want to make an appointment.\n"
"2. **Identify yourself:** Give the required personal details.\n"
"3. **Explain briefly:** State the general reason for the visit.\n"
"4. **Discuss urgency:** Explain whether the issue is routine or needs "
"quicker attention.\n"
"5. **Choose a time:** State your availability and select an appointment.\n"
"6. **Ask practical questions:** Confirm the location, appointment type, "
"costs, and required documents.\n"
"7. **Repeat the details:** Confirm the date, time, doctor, and next steps.\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’d like to make an appointment about recurring headaches. It is not an "
"emergency, but I would like to see a doctor this week. I’m available after "
"three on Wednesday or Friday.”\n"
"\n"
"## Practice Scenario\n"
"\n"
"In this roleplay, you are calling Dr. Avery’s office to arrange a medical "
"appointment. The AI receptionist will ask for your details, the general "
"reason for the visit, and your availability.\n"
"\n"
"During the conversation, try to:\n"
"\n"
"- State that you would like to make an appointment.\n"
"- Provide your name and any requested patient details.\n"
"- Briefly explain the reason for the visit.\n"
"- Say whether the problem is routine or needs quicker attention.\n"
"- Ask about in-person, telephone, or video appointment options.\n"
"- Compare at least two available times.\n"
"- Ask what documents or information you should bring.\n"
"- Confirm the appointment date, time, doctor, location, and next steps.\n"
"\n"
"Focus on communicating the necessary information clearly. You do not need "
"to describe private medical details or use advanced medical vocabulary."
msgstr ""
"医師の予約を取ることは、通常、受付担当者との短い会話を伴います。名前を伝えたり、訪問の大まかな理由を説明したり、利用可能な時間を選択したり、場所や必要な"
"書類などの実務的な詳細を確認したりする必要があります。\n"
"\n"
"受付担当者に完全な病歴を説明する必要はありません。予約の種類を選ぶために、大まかで明確な説明で通常は十分です。\n"
"\n"
"このロールプレイは言語練習用です。医療診断や治療のアドバイスを提供するものではありません。医療緊急事態を経験していると思われる場合は、通常の予約を待たず"
"に、地元の緊急サービスに連絡してください。\n"
"\n"
"## 電話を始める\n"
"\n"
"以下から始めることができます：\n"
"\n"
"- 「こんにちは、予約を取りたいのですが。」\n"
"- 「医師の予約を取るために電話しています。」\n"
"- 「医療相談の予約を取りたいのですが。」\n"
"- 「子供のために予約を取る必要があります。」\n"
"- 「フォローアップの予約を手配したいのですが。」\n"
"- 「再度の訪問をスケジュールするように言われました。」\n"
"\n"
"受付担当者が尋ねるかもしれません：\n"
"\n"
"- 「このクリニックの患者さんですか？」\n"
"- 「お名前を教えていただけますか？」\n"
"- 「生年月日は？」\n"
"- 「どの医師にお会いになられたいですか？」\n"
"- 「予約の理由は何ですか？」\n"
"- 「いつご都合が良いですか？」\n"
"\n"
"## 個人情報を提供する\n"
"\n"
"受付担当者はあなたの患者記録を見つけるために、または新たに作成するために情報が必要な場合があります。\n"
"\n"
"依頼されるかもしれない情報：\n"
"\n"
"- 氏名\n"
"- 生年月日\n"
"- 電話番号\n"
"- 住所\n"
"- 患者番号または保険番号\n"
"- メールアドレス\n"
"- 担当医の名前\n"
"\n"
"便利なフレーズ：\n"
"\n"
"- 「私の名前はアレックス・デモウスキーです。」\n"
"- 「生年月日は1990年5月12日です。」\n"
"- 「すでにクリニックに登録しています。」\n"
"- 「ここでの初めての予約です。」\n"
"- 「私の情報がすでにシステムにあるかどうか確認していただけますか？」\n"
"- 「最近電話番号が変わりました。」\n"
"- 「姓を綴ってもよろしいですか？」\n"
"\n"
"電話で情報を綴る場合：\n"
"\n"
"> 「それはデルタのD、マイクのMとして…」\n"
"\n"
"数字を確認するには：\n"
"\n"
"- 「それは1-5です、5-0ではありません。」\n"
"- 「番号を繰り返しますね。」\n"
"- 「完全な電話番号を取得しましたか？」\n"
"- 「それを読み返していただけますか？」\n"
"\n"
"## 予約の理由を説明する\n"
"\n"
"受付担当者は通常、適切な医師、予約の種類、緊急性を判断するために短い説明を必要とします。\n"
"\n"
"以下を言うことができます：\n"
"\n"
"- 「数日間咳が続いています。」\n"
"- 「背中の痛みを経験しています。」\n"
"- 「繰り返す頭痛について相談したいです。」\n"
"- 「定期健診が必要です。」\n"
"- 「処方を更新する必要があります。」\n"
"- 「検査結果について話し合いたいです。」\n"
"- 「前回の予約後のフォローアップが必要です。」\n"
"- 「医師に診てもらいたい皮膚の問題があります。」\n"
"- 「医療証明書が必要です。」\n"
"- 「予防接種についてお尋ねしたいです。」\n"
"- 「昨日から始まった問題について電話しています。」\n"
"\n"
"役立つ構造：\n"
"\n"
"> 「[一般的な症状または問題]を[期間]間経験しており、医師に診てもらいたいです。」\n"
"\n"
"例えば：\n"
"\n"
"> 「肩の痛みが1週間ほど続いており、改善していません。」\n"
"\n"
"受付担当者に親密または詳細な情報を与える必要はありません。以下を言うことができます：\n"
"\n"
"- 「プライベートな医療問題です。」\n"
"- 「詳細は直接医師と話したいです。」\n"
"- 「個人的な健康問題に関するものであることを記録していただけますか？」\n"
"- 「予約には一般的な説明で十分ですか？」\n"
"\n"
"## 緊急性を説明する\n"
"\n"
"受付担当者は問題の緊急性を尋ねるかもしれません。\n"
"\n"
"便利なフレーズ：\n"
"\n"
"- 「緊急ではありませんが、できるだけ早く診てもらいたいです。」\n"
"- 「症状が悪化しています。」\n"
"- 「かなりの不快感があります。」\n"
"- 「問題が数日間続いているため心配しています。」\n"
"- 「医師から緊急のフォローアップを手配するよう言われました。」\n"
"- 「通常の予約で十分だと思います。」\n"
"- 「緊急性があるかどうか分かりません。」\n"
"- 「看護師が早めの予約が必要かどうか話すために電話してくれませんか？」\n"
"\n"
"受付担当者は以下を提供するかもしれません：\n"
"\n"
"- 通常の予約\n"
"- 当日の予約\n"
"- 緊急予約\n"
"- 電話での相談\n"
"- ビデオでの相談\n"
"- 看護師による相談\n"
"- 他の空いている医師との予約\n"
"\n"
"受付担当者は問題を診断する資格があるわけではありません。彼らの役割は通常、適切なサービスに導くために十分な情報を集めることです。\n"
"\n"
"## 緊急の指示を理解する\n"
"\n"
"診療所は、症状が即時に危険に見える場合、予約を待たずに緊急サービスに連絡するよう指示することがあります。\n"
"\n"
"実際の電話では、クリニックの指示に従ってください。言語学習シミュレーションに頼って緊急性を判断しないでください。\n"
"\n"
"便利なフレーズ：\n"
"\n"
"- 「予約を待つべきだと思いますか？」\n"
"- 「まず看護師と話すべきですか？」\n"
"- 「連絡すべき緊急医療サービスがありますか？」\n"
"- 「緊急の指示を繰り返していただけますか？」\n"
"- 「どの番号に電話すればよいですか？」\n"
"- 「サービスの名前を教えていただけますか？」\n"
"\n"
"誰かの生命や安全に即時の危険があると信じる場合は、地元の緊急サービスに連絡してください。\n"
"\n"
"## 正しい予約の種類を選ぶ\n"
"\n"
"異なる懸念には異なる種類の予約が必要になる場合があります。\n"
"\n"
"一般的な選択肢には次のものがあります：\n"
"\n"
"- **通常の予約** — 緊急性のない医療問題に\n"
"- **緊急の予約** — より迅速な評価が必要な問題に\n"
"- **フォローアップの予約** — 前回の訪問後の進歩を確認するため\n"
"- **電話での相談** — 電話での医師との会話\n"
"- **ビデオでの相談** — ビデオを通じたオンラインの予約\n"
"- **対面の相談** — 診療所での訪問\n"
"- **看護師の予約** — 包帯、注射、または一部の定期的な検査のようなサービスのため\n"
"- **専門医の予約** — 特定の医療分野の医師との相談\n"
"\n"
"便利な質問：\n"
"\n"
"- 「対面の予約が必要ですか？」\n"
"- 「電話で対処できますか？」\n"
"- 「ビデオでの相談は可能ですか？」\n"
"- 「医者または看護師と予約すべきですか？」\n"
"- 「専門医に会うための紹介が必要ですか？」\n"
"- 「どの医師でも対応できますか、または担当医に会うべきですか？」\n"
"- 「予約はどのくらいの時間ですか？」\n"
"- 「この問題に適したタイプの予約ですか？」\n"
"\n"
"## 特定の医師を要求する\n"
"\n"
"定期的に担当している医師や特定の専門分野を持つ医師に会いたい場合があります。\n"
"\n"
"以下を言うことができます：\n"
"\n"
"- 「Dr. Averyに会いたいです。」\n"
"- 「私の担当医は空いていますか？」\n"
"- 「以前この問題についてDr. Averyに診てもらいました。」\n"
"- 「女性医師との予約をお願いできますか？」\n"
"- 「男性医師との予約をお願いできますか？」\n"
"- 「英語を話す医師はいますか？」\n"
"- 「皮膚科医の予約が必要です。」\n"
"- 「空いているどの医師でも構いません。」\n"
"- 「早めの予約が取れるなら、他の医師でも大丈夫です。」\n"
"\n"
"受付担当者の応答：\n"
"\n"
"- 「今週は担当医が空いていません。」\n"
"- 「別の医師が明日お見えになります。」\n"
"- 「Dr. Averyとの最も早い予約は来週の火曜日です。」\n"
"- 「その専門医に会う前に紹介が必要です。」\n"
"\n"
"## 利用可能な時間を伝える\n"
"\n"
"具体的な日付や時間を伝えることが効果的です。\n"
"\n"
"便利なフレーズ：\n"
"\n"
"- 「月曜日の午後は空いています。」\n"
"- 「今週は午前中ならいつでも大丈夫です。」\n"
"- 「午後５時以降は何かありますか？」\n"
"- 「午後３時以前は空いていません。」\n"
"- 「ランチタイムに伺えますか？」\n"
"- 「一番早い予約が希望です。」\n"
"- 「今日何か空いていますか？」\n"
"- 「明日の朝予約がありますか？」\n"
"- 「時間には柔軟に対応できます。」\n"
"- 「木曜日以外ならいつでも空いています。」\n"
"\n"
"受付担当者：\n"
"\n"
"> 「水曜日の10時20分か金曜日の3時45分の予約があります。」\n"
"\n"
"応答：\n"
"\n"
"- 「水曜日の10時20分で大丈夫です。」\n"
"- 「もっと早い時間があるかどうか確認していただけますか？」\n"
"- 「金曜日のほうがいいです。」\n"
"- 「その時間は仕事なので、残念です。」\n"
"- 「もっと遅い時間はありませんか？」\n"
"- 「一番早い時間でお願いします。」\n"
"\n"
"## 日付と時間を正確に確認する\n"
"\n"
"電話での日付や時間は理解するのが難しい場合があります。常に確認を行います。\n"
"\n"
"便利なフレーズ：\n"
"\n"
"- 「火曜日の14日でしたか？」\n"
"- 「9時15分それとも9時50分でしたか？」\n"
"- 「時間をゆっくりと繰り返していただけますか？」\n"
"- 「金曜日の2時半で間違いありませんか？」\n"
"- 「24時間表記でお願いできますか？」\n"
"- 「その予約は午前中、それとも午後ですか？」\n"
"- 「確認のメッセージを送ってもらえますか？」\n"
"\n"
"最終の詳細を繰り返すことが有効です：\n"
"\n"
"> 「確認します：7月14日、火曜日、3時30分、Dr. Avery。」\n"
"\n"
"## 場所について質問する\n"
"\n"
"一部のクリニックは複数の建物や場所で運営されています。\n"
"\n"
"質問することができます：\n"
"\n"
"- 「予約はどのクリニックですか？」\n"
"- 「住所を教えていただけますか？」\n"
"- 「どの階に行けばよいですか？」\n"
"- 「どの受付を使用すればよいですか？」\n"
"- 「入口はバリアフリーですか？」\n"
"- 「近くに駐車場はありますか？」\n"
"- 「何分前に到着するのが理想ですか？」\n"
"- 「どこでチェックインすればよいですか？」\n"
"- 「予約はメインクリニックですか、それとも専門センターですか？」\n"
"\n"
"## 持参品について尋ねる\n"
"\n"
"予約によっては書類、薬の情報、検査結果を持参する必要があります。\n"
"\n"
"便利な質問：\n"
"\n"
"- 「何を持参すればよいですか？」\n"
"- 「身分証明が必要ですか？」\n"
"- 「保険証を持参するべきですか？」\n"
"- 「紹介状が必要ですか？」\n"
"- 「以前の検査結果を持参するべきですか？」\n"
"- 「現在服用中の薬のリストが必要ですか？」\n"
"- 「予約前に何か準備すべきですか？」\n"
"- 「訪問前に何も食べてはいけませんか？」\n"
"- 「指示をメールで送ってもらえますか？」\n"
"\n"
"推測に基づいて断食や薬の中止、治療の変更を行わないでください。特定の指示についてクリニックに確認を求めてください。\n"
"\n"
"## 費用と保険について尋ねる\n"
"\n"
"予約が保険でカバーされているか、支払いが必要かどうかを確認する必要があるかもしれません。\n"
"\n"
"便利な質問：\n"
"\n"
"- 「この予約は私の保険でカバーされていますか？」\n"
"- 「私の保険提供者を受け入れていますか？」\n"
"- 「相談料はありますか？」\n"
"- 「予約の費用はいくらですか？」\n"
"- 「前払いが必要ですか？」\n"
"- 「カードで支払えますか？」\n"
"- 「請求書を受け取りますか？」\n"
"- 「保険会社からの承認が必要ですか？」\n"
"- 「キャンセル料はありますか？」\n"
"\n"
"受付担当者は、カバー状況を確認するために、あなたの保険番号や患者番号が必要かもしれません。\n"
"\n"
"## 言語サポートを依頼する\n"
"\n"
"現地の言語に自信がない場合は、言語サポートが利用可能かどうか問い合わせてください。\n"
"\n"
"以下を言うことができます：\n"
"\n"
"- 「英語を話す医師はいますか？」\n"
"- 「通訳は利用可能ですか？」\n"
"- 「翻訳を手伝う人を連れて行ってもいいですか？」\n"
"- 「予約は英語で行えますか？」\n"
"- 「もう少しゆっくり話していただけますか？」\n"
"- 「多少ポーランド語は理解できますが、医療用語にヘルプが必要かもしれません。」\n"
"- 「重要な情報を文書で送っていただけますか？」\n"
"\n"
"別の人が予約に参加できるかどうか事前に確認してください。\n"
"\n"
"## アクセシビリティサポートを依頼する\n"
"\n"
"予約を取る際にアクセシビリティニーズについてクリニックに知らせることができます。\n"
"\n"
"便利なフレーズ：\n"
"\n"
"- 「車椅子を使用しています。クリニックはバリアフリーですか？」\n"
"- 「段差のないアクセスが必要です。」\n"
"- 「電話での聞こえにくさがあります。」\n"
"- 「医師が書面でコミュニケーションを取ることができますか？」\n"
"- 「予約に追加の時間が必要です。」\n"
"- 「誰かが建物に入るのを手伝ってくれませんか？」\n"
"- 「バリアフリートイレはありますか？」\n"
"- 「予約にアクセスニーズを記録してくれませんか？」\n"
"\n"
"## 他の人のために予約を取る\n"
"\n"
"子供、家族、あるいはサポートしている人のために予約を手配するかもしれません。\n"
"\n"
"以下を言うことができます：\n"
"\n"
"- 「息子のために予約を取りたいのですが。」\n"
"- 「母のために予約を手配しています。」\n"
"- 「患者さんの名前は…」\n"
"- 「予約を手配する許可があります。」\n"
"- 「患者さんが直接お話しする必要がありますか？」\n"
"- 「同意が必要ですか？」\n"
"- 「彼らと一緒に予約に参加できますか？」\n"
"\n"
"プライバシーに関する規則により、患者さんの同意なしにクリニックが話し合える内容が制限される場合があります。\n"
"\n"
"## 予約の変更\n"
"\n"
"参加できない場合は、できるだけ早くクリニックに連絡してください。\n"
"\n"
"便利なフレーズ：\n"
"\n"
"- 「予約を変更する必要があります。」\n"
"- 「その時間には空いていません。」\n"
"- 「別の日に予約を変更できますか？」\n"
"- 「来週何か空いていますか？」\n"
"- 「電話での相談に変更できますか？」\n"
"- 「同じ医師のままでいたいです。」\n"
"- 「最も早い別の予約はいつですか？」\n"
"\n"
"提供する必要があるかもしれません：\n"
"\n"
"- 氏名\n"
"- 生年月日\n"
"- 元々の予約日\n"
"- 医師の名前\n"
"- 患者番号または予約番号\n"
"\n"
"## 予約のキャンセル\n"
"\n"
"キャンセルしたいと言う：\n"
"\n"
"- 「予約をキャンセルする必要があります。」\n"
"- 「参加できません。」\n"
"- 「予約は月曜日の2時です。」\n"
"- 「キャンセルされたことを確認していただけますか？」\n"
"- 「キャンセル料はありますか？」\n"
"- 「今すぐ別の予約を取る必要がありますか？」\n"
"- 「キャンセルの確認を送っていただけますか？」\n"
"\n"
"早めのキャンセルは、他の患者さんが予約を利用できる可能性を提供します。\n"
"\n"
"## キャンセル待ちリストに参加する\n"
"\n"
"適切な予約がない場合、待機またはキャンセルリストがあるかどうかを問い合わせてください。\n"
"\n"
"便利なフレーズ：\n"
"\n"
"- 「キャンセル待ちリストに追加してもらえますか？」\n"
"- 「早めの予約が可能になったら連絡してください。」\n"
"- 「短期間で参加できます。」\n"
"- 「どのように連絡を受けますか？」\n"
"- 「どのくらいの速さで対応が必要ですか？」\n"
"- 「早めの予約を待ちながら、現在の予約を残してくれますか？」\n"
"\n"
"予約がすぐに取れない場合の対応\n"
"\n"
"受付担当者が言うかもしれません：\n"
"\n"
"- 「今日は予約が空いていません。」\n"
"- 「医師は完全に予約されています。」\n"
"- 「次の空いている予約は2週間後です。」\n"
"- 「担当医は現在不在です。」\n"
"- 「電話での相談のみがあります。」\n"
"\n"
"応答：\n"
"\n"
"- 「別の医師は空いていますか？」\n"
"- 「看護師と相談できますか？」\n"
"- 「他のクリニックに連絡できますか？」\n"
"- 「キャンセル待ちリストに追加してもらえますか？」\n"
"- 「症状が悪化した場合はどうすればよいですか？」\n"
"- 「緊急医療サービスはありますか？」\n"
"- 「最初に電話での相談を受けることができますか？」\n"
"\n"
"## 予約を確認する\n"
"\n"
"電話を終える前に、以下を確認してください：\n"
"\n"
"- 患者さんの名前\n"
"- 医師または医療専門家\n"
"- 日付\n"
"- 時間\n"
"- 予約の種類\n"
"- 場所または通話方法\n"
"- 持参すべきもの\n"
"- 準備に必要な指示\n"
"- キャンセルポリシー\n"
"\n"
"以下を言うことができます：\n"
"\n"
"- 「すべての詳細を確認できますか？」\n"
"- 「誰に会えますか？」\n"
"- 「これは対面ですか、それとも電話の予約ですか？」\n"
"- 「医師が電話してくれるのですか、またはクリニックに電話すべきですか？」\n"
"- 「医師が使用する番号はどれですか？」\n"
"- 「早めに到着するべきですか？」\n"
"- 「テキストやメールでの確認を受け取りますか？」\n"
"- 「キャンセルが必要な場合はどうすればよいですか？」\n"
"\n"
"## 単純な予約の会話\n"
"\n"
"典型的な会話は次のようになるかもしれません：\n"
"\n"
"> **受付担当者:** おはようございます、Dr. Averyのオフィスです。お手伝いできますか？  \n"
"> **患者さん:** こんにちは、予約を取りたいのですが。  \n"
"> **受付担当者:** もちろんです。このクリニックにすでに登録していますか？  \n"
"> **患者さん:** はい。私の名前はアレックス・デモウスキーです。  \n"
"> **受付担当者:** ありがとうございます。予約の一般的な理由は何ですか？  \n"
"> **患者さん:** 肩の痛みが1週間ほど続いており、改善していません。  \n"
"> **受付担当者:** 対面の予約を希望しますか？  \n"
"> **患者さん:** はい、お願いします。今週空いている時間はありますか？  \n"
"> **受付担当者:** 木曜日の11時20分か、金曜日の4時10分があります。  \n"
"> **患者さん:** 金曜日の4時10分の方が良いです。  \n"
"> **受付担当者:** それは中央クリニックでのDr. Averyとの予約になります。  \n"
"> **患者さん:** いいですね。何か持って行くべきものはありますか？  \n"
"> **受付担当者:** 身分証明書と現在服用中の薬のリストを持参してください。  \n"
"> **患者さん:** 確認させてください：金曜日の4時10分に中央クリニックでDr. Averyに。  \n"
"> **受付担当者:** その通りです。\n"
"\n"
"## 単純な予約の公式\n"
"\n"
"予約を取るときは次の構造に従います：\n"
"\n"
"1. **リクエスト:** 予約を取りたいと言う。\n"
"2. **自己を特定する:** 必要な個人情報を提供する。\n"
"3. **簡単に説明:** 訪問の大まかな理由を伝える。\n"
"4. **緊急性を話し合う:** 問題が通常のものか、それとも早めの対応が必要かを説明する。\n"
"5. **時間を選ぶ:** 空いている時間を伝えて予約を選ぶ。\n"
"6. **実践的な質問をする:** 場所、予約の種類、費用、必要な書類を確認する。\n"
"7. **詳細を繰り返す:** 日付、時間、医師と次のステップを確認する。\n"
"\n"
"例えば：\n"
"\n"
"> 「再発する頭痛についての予約を取りたいのですが。緊急ではありませんが、今週医師に診てもらいたいです。水曜日または金曜日の3時以降に空いています。」\n"
"\n"
"## 練習シナリオ\n"
"\n"
"このロールプレイでは、Dr. "
"Averyのオフィスに電話をかけて医療の予約を設定します。AI受付担当者が詳細、訪問の一般的理由、利用可能な時間を尋ねます。\n"
"\n"
"会話中に、以下を試みてください：\n"
"\n"
"- 予約をしたいと述べる。\n"
"- 名前や必要な患者の詳細を提供する。\n"
"- 訪問理由を簡単に説明する。\n"
"- 問題が通常のものか、それとも早めの対応が必要か言う。\n"
"- 対面、電話、またはビデオの予約オプションについて尋ねる。\n"
"- 利用可能な時間を少なくとも2つ比較する。\n"
"- 持参すべき書類や情報について尋ねる。\n"
"- 予約の日付、時間、医師、場所、次のステップを確認する。\n"
"\n"
"必要な情報を明確に伝えることに焦点を当ててください。プライベートな医療の詳細を詳しく述べたり、高度な医療用語を使用したりする必要はありません。"

